"""
Current that carries a fixed power at the measured terminal voltage: y = P / max(u, 1 V).

Ports: `u` terminal voltage [V], `y` current [A].

The one-volt floor on the denominator keeps the current finite while the voltage starts at or
passes through zero; above 1 V it does not act. The sign of `P` carries through, so the block
serves charging and discharging alike.
"""
component TerminalPowerCurrent
  extends BlockComponents.Interfaces.SISO
  "Power to carry"
  parameter P::Power = 20000.0
relations
  y = P / max(u, 1.0)
end
